00:04:51.986 --> 00:04:52.487
started

00:04:52.487 --> 00:04:53.121
this company

00:04:53.121 --> 00:04:54.155
in Gradium.

00:04:54.155 --> 00:04:55.389
So what made

00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:55.756
you make

00:04:55.756 --> 00:04:56.457
this decision?

00:04:56.457 --> 00:04:56.791
Going

00:04:56.791 --> 00:04:57.158
from a

00:04:57.158 --> 00:04:58.325
research lab

00:04:58.325 --> 00:04:59.393
to getting into

00:04:59.393 --> 00:05:00.027
the monetization

00:05:00.027 --> 00:05:00.927
side and opening

00:05:00.927 --> 00:05:01.094
a

00:05:01.094 --> 00:05:03.797
commercial company?

00:05:03.797 --> 00:05:05.565
So the story

00:05:05.565 --> 00:05:07.433
of, of,

00:05:07.433 --> 00:05:07.967
Gradium

00:05:07.967 --> 00:05:09.235
and Kyutai starts

00:05:09.235 --> 00:05:09.768
even before.

00:05:09.768 --> 00:05:10.769
So my co-founders

00:05:10.769 --> 00:05:11.670
and I,

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.304
we used to work

00:05:12.304 --> 00:05:12.738
at Google

00:05:12.738 --> 00:05:15.473
and Meta and we

00:05:15.473 --> 00:05:16.307
so we used

00:05:16.307 --> 00:05:16.775
to work

00:05:16.775 --> 00:05:17.175
in the team

00:05:17.175 --> 00:05:17.875
of Yann LeCun

00:05:17.875 --> 00:05:18.343
at meta.

00:05:18.343 --> 00:05:19.110
And then

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:19.610
I moved to

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.611
Google Brain,

00:05:20.611 --> 00:05:21.445
and it was

00:05:21.445 --> 00:05:22.146
an environment

00:05:22.146 --> 00:05:23.514
where we are

00:05:23.514 --> 00:05:23.947
doing a lot

00:05:23.947 --> 00:05:25.315
of discoveries,

00:05:25.315 --> 00:05:25.949
and we are

00:05:25.949 --> 00:05:26.516
sharing it

00:05:26.516 --> 00:05:26.783
through

00:05:26.783 --> 00:05:27.217
scientific

00:05:27.217 --> 00:05:28.118
publications

00:05:28.118 --> 00:05:28.852
and open source

00:05:28.852 --> 00:05:29.185
and so on

00:05:29.185 --> 00:05:29.686
and so forth.

00:05:31.187 --> 00:05:31.821
The relation

00:05:31.821 --> 00:05:32.421
to open source

00:05:32.421 --> 00:05:33.189
in big companies

00:05:33.189 --> 00:05:33.556
kind of

00:05:33.556 --> 00:05:33.856
changed

00:05:33.856 --> 00:05:34.890
after ChatGPT.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:35.624
So we decided

00:05:35.624 --> 00:05:36.091
to recreate

00:05:36.091 --> 00:05:36.825
an environment

00:05:36.825 --> 00:05:37.493
that looked more

00:05:37.493 --> 00:05:37.926
like what

00:05:37.926 --> 00:05:38.327
we liked,

00:05:38.327 --> 00:05:39.061
which is

00:05:39.061 --> 00:05:39.461
purely

00:05:39.461 --> 00:05:40.295
dedicated to

00:05:40.295 --> 00:05:41.096
open research.

00:05:41.096 --> 00:05:43.031
And so in 2023,

00:05:43.031 --> 00:05:43.831
we created Kyutai

00:05:43.831 --> 00:05:44.232
as a

00:05:44.232 --> 00:05:44.832
nonprofit lab

00:05:44.832 --> 00:05:45.366
because we didn't

00:05:45.366 --> 00:05:45.633
want to

00:05:45.633 --> 00:05:46.067
make products.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:46.701
We just wanted

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:47.368
to make

00:05:47.368 --> 00:05:48.168
open research,

00:05:48.168 --> 00:05:48.936
open source,

00:05:48.936 --> 00:05:50.871
open models.

00:05:50.871 --> 00:05:51.405
Exactly.

00:05:51.405 --> 00:05:52.005
And share

00:05:52.005 --> 00:05:52.973
every discovery

00:05:52.973 --> 00:05:53.807
with the world

00:05:53.807 --> 00:05:54.808
without bothering

00:05:54.808 --> 00:05:55.375
with a

00:05:55.375 --> 00:05:56.609
IP and so on.

00:05:56.609 --> 00:05:57.276
Right.

00:05:57.276 --> 00:05:58.744
So we got

00:05:58.744 --> 00:05:59.211
back then

00:05:59.211 --> 00:06:00.546
€300 million

00:06:00.546 --> 00:06:01.714
of donation,

00:06:01.714 --> 00:06:02.548
not investment

00:06:02.548 --> 00:06:03.315
donation

00:06:03.315 --> 00:06:03.849
from Eric

00:06:03.849 --> 00:06:04.149
Schmidt,

00:06:04.149 --> 00:06:04.449
the former

00:06:04.449 --> 00:06:06.084
CEO of Google,

00:06:06.084 --> 00:06:06.785
and others

00:06:06.785 --> 00:06:07.018
who are

00:06:07.018 --> 00:06:07.585
two French,

00:06:08.286 --> 00:06:08.987
a very

00:06:08.987 --> 00:06:09.487
successful

00:06:09.487 --> 00:06:10.688
businessman.

00:06:10.688 --> 00:06:11.622
And we started

00:06:11.622 --> 00:06:11.989
working on

00:06:11.989 --> 00:06:12.656
real time dialog

00:06:12.656 --> 00:06:12.890
because

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.290
nobody was

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:14.091
working on that.

00:06:14.091 --> 00:06:14.725
So we shipped

00:06:14.725 --> 00:06:15.692
machine 2024,

00:06:15.692 --> 00:06:16.059
which was the

00:06:16.059 --> 00:06:16.426
first real-time

00:06:16.426 --> 00:06:17.060
conversational

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:17.627
model.

00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:18.595
It was already

00:06:18.595 --> 00:06:19.229
what we now

00:06:19.229 --> 00:06:19.929
everybody knows

00:06:19.929 --> 00:06:20.730
under the name

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:21.497
Full Duplex

00:06:21.497 --> 00:06:22.065
that nobody

00:06:22.065 --> 00:06:23.499
knew back then

00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:24.066
for a very

00:06:24.066 --> 00:06:24.533
long time,

00:06:24.533 --> 00:06:25.167
almost two years.

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:25.434
It was

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:26.135
the only model

00:06:26.135 --> 00:06:26.669
that was

00:06:26.669 --> 00:06:27.169
full duplex

00:06:27.169 --> 00:06:27.903
in the world.

00:06:27.903 --> 00:06:28.237
And

00:06:28.237 --> 00:06:28.870
interestingly,

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:29.738
we published it.

00:06:29.738 --> 00:06:31.072
We made a paper.

00:06:31.072 --> 00:06:32.073
Open

00:06:32.073 --> 00:06:33.107
source models

00:06:33.107 --> 00:06:33.608
that were

00:06:33.608 --> 00:06:34.075
downloaded

00:06:34.075 --> 00:06:34.776
40 million

00:06:34.776 --> 00:06:35.343
of times

00:06:35.343 --> 00:06:36.544
over two years.

00:06:36.544 --> 00:06:37.111
And then

00:06:37.111 --> 00:06:37.578
we started

00:06:37.578 --> 00:06:38.145
to get a lot

00:06:38.145 --> 00:06:38.946
of inbound

00:06:38.946 --> 00:06:39.646
traction

00:06:39.646 --> 00:06:41.114
that we could not

00:06:41.114 --> 00:06:41.648
answer to

00:06:41.648 --> 00:06:42.349
as a nonprofit.

00:06:42.349 --> 00:06:43.383
So companies

00:06:43.383 --> 00:06:44.517
would ask us

00:06:44.517 --> 00:06:44.918
to make

00:06:44.918 --> 00:06:45.885
a more polished,

00:06:45.885 --> 00:06:46.619
more professional

00:06:46.619 --> 00:06:46.986
version

00:06:46.986 --> 00:06:47.453
of our open

00:06:47.453 --> 00:06:47.987
source models.

00:06:47.987 --> 00:06:48.287
And we are

00:06:48.287 --> 00:06:48.621
saying, no,

00:06:48.621 --> 00:06:49.021
we are not

00:06:49.021 --> 00:06:49.355
profit.

00:06:49.355 --> 00:06:49.889
We're not fit

00:06:49.889 --> 00:06:50.823
for profit.

00:06:50.823 --> 00:06:51.423
And we were

00:06:51.423 --> 00:06:53.392
seeing the voice

00:06:53.392 --> 00:06:54.459
as a category

00:06:54.459 --> 00:06:55.494
just exploding.

00:06:55.494 --> 00:06:55.894
And at the

00:06:55.894 --> 00:06:56.428
same time,

00:06:57.429 --> 00:06:58.263
it was a bit

00:06:58.263 --> 00:06:58.730
weird to

00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:59.797
not get

00:06:59.797 --> 00:07:00.631
into the arena

00:07:00.631 --> 00:07:01.699
of what works

00:07:01.699 --> 00:07:02.166
like what

00:07:02.166 --> 00:07:02.533
matters

00:07:02.533 --> 00:07:02.967
in the end,

00:07:02.967 --> 00:07:04.902
which is now.

00:07:04.902 --> 00:07:05.469
I realize

00:07:05.469 --> 00:07:05.869
everybody

00:07:05.869 --> 00:07:06.370
is excited

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:06.870
when you open

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:07.371
source software

00:07:07.371 --> 00:07:07.571
because

00:07:07.571 --> 00:07:08.939
it's free, right?

00:07:08.939 --> 00:07:09.406
It's much

00:07:09.406 --> 00:07:09.939
more difficult

00:07:09.939 --> 00:07:10.540
to make a model

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:10.907
that people

00:07:10.907 --> 00:07:12.308
will pay for that

00:07:12.308 --> 00:07:13.009
an open source.

00:07:13.009 --> 00:07:13.509
So even the

00:07:13.509 --> 00:07:14.010
scientific

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:14.877
challenge of

00:07:14.877 --> 00:07:16.178
being the best

00:07:16.178 --> 00:07:16.912
at commercial

00:07:16.912 --> 00:07:18.180
voice models

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.181
was the natural

00:07:19.181 --> 00:07:19.581
next step

00:07:19.581 --> 00:07:20.148
after what

00:07:20.148 --> 00:07:20.582
we had done.

00:07:20.582 --> 00:07:22.117
And so we created

00:07:22.117 --> 00:07:22.550
Gradium

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:23.518
as a spin off.

00:07:23.518 --> 00:07:23.885
It's an

00:07:23.885 --> 00:07:24.385
independent

00:07:24.385 --> 00:07:24.752
structure

00:07:24.752 --> 00:07:25.053
from the

00:07:25.053 --> 00:07:25.386
nonprofit

00:07:25.386 --> 00:07:26.020
Kyutai is

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:26.487
still doing

00:07:26.487 --> 00:07:26.854
research.

00:07:26.854 --> 00:07:27.088
We have

00:07:27.088 --> 00:07:27.621
partnerships

00:07:27.621 --> 00:07:28.022
between the

00:07:28.022 --> 00:07:28.856
two organization.

00:07:28.856 --> 00:07:29.156
Oh yeah.

00:07:29.156 --> 00:07:29.957
Absolutely.

00:07:29.957 --> 00:07:30.357
And Kyutai

00:07:30.357 --> 00:07:30.791
is working

00:07:30.791 --> 00:07:31.425
also on world

00:07:31.425 --> 00:07:32.225
models,

00:07:32.225 --> 00:07:33.326
on many things

00:07:33.326 --> 00:07:33.994
that have nothing

00:07:33.994 --> 00:07:34.194
to do

00:07:34.194 --> 00:07:35.428
with speech.

00:07:35.428 --> 00:07:36.462
But at Gradium

00:07:36.462 --> 00:07:36.829
we really

00:07:36.829 --> 00:07:37.597
only focus

00:07:37.597 --> 00:07:38.598
on voice models.

00:07:38.598 --> 00:07:39.031
And we have

00:07:39.031 --> 00:07:39.365
developed

00:07:39.365 --> 00:07:40.633
a lot of

00:07:40.633 --> 00:07:41.500
new technologies

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.168
that we that,

00:07:43.168 --> 00:07:43.435
you know,

00:07:43.435 --> 00:07:44.036
bridge the gap

00:07:44.036 --> 00:07:44.336
between

00:07:44.336 --> 00:07:44.937
open source

00:07:44.937 --> 00:07:45.537
and something

00:07:45.537 --> 00:07:46.104
that will

00:07:46.104 --> 00:07:46.671
actually work

00:07:46.671 --> 00:07:47.172
in position.

00:07:47.172 --> 00:07:48.706
For example,

00:07:48.706 --> 00:07:49.807
a lot of

00:07:49.807 --> 00:07:50.208
work around

00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:50.775
post training.

00:07:50.775 --> 00:07:51.375
So, you know,

00:07:51.375 --> 00:07:53.711
in the end,

00:07:53.711 --> 00:07:54.011
what's

00:07:54.011 --> 00:07:54.511
interesting

00:07:54.511 --> 00:07:54.979
about voice

00:07:54.979 --> 00:07:55.379
is like,

00:07:55.379 --> 00:07:55.779
it's not

00:07:55.779 --> 00:07:56.513
a verifiable

00:07:56.513 --> 00:07:57.381
problem.

00:07:57.381 --> 00:07:58.048
So you cannot

00:07:58.048 --> 00:07:58.448
just have

00:07:58.448 --> 00:07:58.615
a

00:07:58.615 --> 00:07:59.583
self-improvement

00:07:59.583 --> 00:08:00.550
loop with LLMs

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:01.017
right?

00:08:01.017 --> 00:08:01.518
You need to have

00:08:01.518 --> 00:08:02.218
human feedback

00:08:02.218 --> 00:08:02.819
constantly in

00:08:02.819 --> 00:08:03.353
the development.

00:08:03.353 --> 00:08:04.854
So we are working

00:08:04.854 --> 00:08:05.554
with very

00:08:05.554 --> 00:08:06.188
tight feedback

00:08:06.188 --> 00:08:06.989
from human

00:08:06.989 --> 00:08:08.257
annotators

00:08:08.257 --> 00:08:09.424
to characterize

00:08:09.424 --> 00:08:09.591
the

00:08:09.591 --> 00:08:10.459
expressiveness,

00:08:10.459 --> 00:08:11.660
the naturalness,

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.194
the pronunciation

00:08:13.194 --> 00:08:13.595
and so on

00:08:13.595 --> 00:08:14.295
and so forth.

00:08:14.295 --> 00:08:14.829
And so we

00:08:14.829 --> 00:08:15.630
iterate on that

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:16.798
and we develop,

00:08:16.798 --> 00:08:17.064
you know,

00:08:17.064 --> 00:08:17.732
new algorithm

00:08:17.732 --> 00:08:18.866
for post training

00:08:18.866 --> 00:08:19.233
to make

00:08:19.233 --> 00:08:19.700
the voices.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:20.167
That sounds the

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:20.901
most natural.

00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:24.704
And this is like

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:25.205
more of a

00:08:25.205 --> 00:08:25.972
casual question

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:26.339
to you.

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:27.340
It's like there's

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:27.707
a naming

00:08:27.707 --> 00:08:28.408
thread running,

00:08:28.408 --> 00:08:28.674
you know,

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:28.875
through

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:29.575
all of this

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:33.379
Kyutai means

00:08:33.445 --> 00:08:33.912
swear

00:08:33.912 --> 00:08:34.813
in Japanese.

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:35.347
Your models

00:08:35.347 --> 00:08:35.747
are named

00:08:35.747 --> 00:08:37.782
Mochi and Hibiki.

00:08:37.782 --> 00:08:38.583
&amp; Gradium’s

00:08:38.583 --> 00:08:39.250
Legal entity

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:39.651
is also

00:08:39.651 --> 00:08:40.618
like sphere

00:08:40.618 --> 00:08:41.886
II, right.

00:08:41.886 --> 00:08:43.087
So where does the

00:08:43.087 --> 00:08:43.654
naming

00:08:43.654 --> 00:08:44.255
coming from?

00:08:44.255 --> 00:08:45.422
Like what is this

00:08:45.422 --> 00:08:46.256
love with

00:08:46.256 --> 00:08:48.625
the Japanese?

00:08:48.625 --> 00:08:49.025
Yeah.

00:08:49.025 --> 00:08:50.493
So actually

00:08:50.493 --> 00:08:50.894
it's very

00:08:50.894 --> 00:08:53.730
trivial. So

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:54.931
the code name

00:08:54.931 --> 00:08:55.665
of Kyutai

00:08:55.665 --> 00:08:56.565
was sphere.

00:08:56.565 --> 00:08:57.333
At first

00:08:57.333 --> 00:08:58.367
it was sphere

00:08:58.367 --> 00:08:59.501
because we met

00:08:59.501 --> 00:09:00.435
in a restaurant

00:09:00.435 --> 00:09:01.269
named sphere.

00:09:01.269 --> 00:09:01.837
So we're like,

00:09:01.837 --> 00:09:02.070
okay,

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:02.437
we call

00:09:02.437 --> 00:09:03.038
the project

00:09:03.038 --> 00:09:05.139
Sphere.

00:09:05.139 --> 00:09:05.573
And then

00:09:05.573 --> 00:09:06.274
we had lawyers

00:09:06.274 --> 00:09:06.741
who told us

00:09:06.741 --> 00:09:07.208
we could not

00:09:07.208 --> 00:09:07.708
trademark

00:09:07.708 --> 00:09:08.809
this name.

00:09:08.809 --> 00:09:09.677
So we looked

00:09:09.677 --> 00:09:10.411
and we ask

00:09:10.411 --> 00:09:11.645
ChatGPT, okay,

00:09:11.645 --> 00:09:12.246
give us

00:09:12.246 --> 00:09:12.613
sphere

00:09:12.613 --> 00:09:13.614
in all languages.

00:09:13.614 --> 00:09:14.681
And we saw that

00:09:14.681 --> 00:09:15.382
Kyutai

00:09:15.382 --> 00:09:16.816
had AI in it

00:09:16.816 --> 00:09:17.383
like, okay,

00:09:17.383 --> 00:09:17.650
you know,

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:18.518
and it's

00:09:18.518 --> 00:09:19.052
a nice thing.

00:09:19.052 --> 00:09:20.219
Then realizes

00:09:20.219 --> 00:09:20.653
there is

00:09:20.653 --> 00:09:21.787
a linguistic

00:09:21.787 --> 00:09:22.655
particularity of

00:09:22.655 --> 00:09:24.056
a Japanese

00:09:24.056 --> 00:09:24.490
is that

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:25.190
it's a very

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.025
simple syllabic

00:09:27.025 --> 00:09:28.393
alphabet.

00:09:28.393 --> 00:09:29.727
So Japanese

00:09:29.727 --> 00:09:30.228
names are

00:09:30.228 --> 00:09:30.628
very easy

00:09:30.628 --> 00:09:31.095
to pronounce

00:09:31.095 --> 00:09:31.529
for everyone

00:09:31.529 --> 00:09:32.029
in the world.

00:09:32.029 --> 00:09:32.396
Right?

00:09:32.396 --> 00:09:32.797
There is no

00:09:32.797 --> 00:09:33.731
complex syllable.

00:09:34.832 --> 00:09:35.966
And so we, we, we

00:09:35.966 --> 00:09:37.367
went to Moshi,

00:09:37.367 --> 00:09:39.102
and then Hibiki

00:09:39.102 --> 00:09:39.503
and then

00:09:39.503 --> 00:09:40.103
we're like, okay,

00:09:40.103 --> 00:09:41.304
